[36.0968, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[27;1H  to discuss three independent design topics.\u001b[40X\u001b[28;85H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\u001b[30;1H\u2022 \u001b(B\u001b[mReady to discuss three independent design topics.\u001b[34X\u001b[31;85H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\r\n  Worked for 5s \u2022 14:01                                                              \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[33;85H\u001b[1K\u001b[1m\u001b[2m\u001b[35;1H\u203a \u001b(B\u001b[mYou are an independent discussion fork. Topic: Runtime flow.\u001b[23X\r\n  Use the source conversation as background; do not continue its unfinished actions. \r\n  Discuss the message below. Do not edit repository files unless the user later asks \r\n  you to implement changes.\u001b[58X\u001b[39;85H\u001b[1K\r\n  Initial message for this fork:\u001b[53X\r\n  In English, suggest two ways to simplify runtime lifecycle states. Start your      \r\n  answer with Runtime:. Max 30 words. Do not use tools.\u001b[30X\u001b[43;85H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\u001b[45;1H\u2022 \u001b(B\u001b[mRuntime: Merge overlapping phases into queued, running, and finished. Store        \r\n  outcomes and retry details separately to avoid multiplying lifecycle states.       \u001b[9;3H\u001b[?12l\u001b[?25h"]
